  "observations": [
    "The first 2048/192m pass produced visible triangular patterns and median 77 FPS versus baseline 92/94.",
    "The 100ms refresh bound recovered much of the rendering cost. Receiver-plane sampling at exact texel centres reduced comparison errors.",
    "The 4096/128m trial improves thin-slat shadows. Some small edge patterns and bright rims remain; wider routes and motion are not yet visually accepted.",
    "Native CPU rays identify nearby GRS III metal slats where the coarse map can miss a caster. Receiver offset and rasterization also affect the comparison; these probes do not establish a single cause for every artifact."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Fixed light direction, matching the current material shader; no dynamic sunlight or night switch yet.",
    "TNT-driven buffer refresh is the intended input path but shadow response to actual TNT has not yet been tested.",
    "Only MapTile meshes cast/receive the trial shadows; vanilla blocks, players and mobs are not included.",
    "The isolated hook runs after the existing map render, so its map applies on the next frame. Production integration still needs to run at the correct point after buffer refresh.",
    "Region switches, disconnect cleanup, resource reloads, exact GL state invariants, camera movement and broad route performance need explicit checks.",
    "The rough horizontal caster bound should be replaced by the actual light frustum before production use.",
    "This is not an installed preview feature or proof of full-campus realism."
  ],
  "nextChecks": [
    "Wire sunlight consistently with the Minecraft sky and disable daytime shadows at night.",
    "Verify actual TNT excavation changes the depth map and restoration restores it in the isolated save.",
    "Add production lifecycle/state handling and inspect representative ground and aerial routes."
  ],
